-# SmartHiscoreLookup
-SmartHiscoreLookup OSRS plugin+# Smart Hiscore Lookup
+
+Smart Hiscore Lookup is a RuneLite external plugin that keeps Old School RuneScape hiscore links close at hand while you play. The current implementation is intentionally lightweight: it normalizes RuneScape display names, builds official hiscore lookup URLs, and shows an optional login reminder with the lookup URL for the local player.
+
+## Features
+
+- RuneLite plugin metadata wired through `runelite-plugin.properties`.
+- Plugin descriptor, package name, Gradle group, and launcher class aligned under `com.itmeansbigmountain.smarthiscorelookup`.
+- Config option to enable or disable the login reminder.
+- Configurable hiscore base URL for official, seasonal, or custom lookup targets.
+- Tested name normalization and URL generation helpers so core behavior can be verified without launching a live RuneLite client.
+
+## Repository layout
+
+```text
+src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/smarthiscorelookup/
+  SmartHiscoreLookupPlugin.java   # RuneLite plugin entry point and hiscore URL helpers
+  SmartHiscoreLookupConfig.java   # RuneLite config panel items
+src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/smarthiscorelookup/
+  SmartHiscoreLookupPluginTest.java # JUnit smoke tests plus the dev-mode RuneLite launcher
+runelite-plugin.properties        # External plugin metadata used by RuneLite/plugin-hub
+plugin.json                       # Project metadata for local tracking
+build.gradle                      # Java 11 RuneLite Gradle build
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Java 11. In this workspace, use:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
+```
+
+- Network access to `https://repo.runelite.net` and Maven Central for dependency resolution.
+
+## Build and test
+
+From the plugin directory:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+Run the plugin in RuneLite developer mode:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew run --no-daemon --args='--developer-mode --debug'
+```
+
+The `run` task loads `SmartHiscoreLookupPluginTest.main`, which registers `SmartHiscoreLookupPlugin` with RuneLite's `ExternalPluginManager` before starting the client.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Show Login Hint | Enabled | Prints a chat message after login with a hiscore lookup URL for the local player. |
+| Hiscore Base URL | `https://secure.runescape.com/m=hiscore_oldschool/hiscorepersonal` | Base URL used when building lookup links. Existing query strings are preserved and `user1=<name>` is appended. |
+
+## API and privacy notes
+
+Smart Hiscore Lookup does not call a third-party API from the plugin. It only builds a RuneScape hiscore URL locally from the player name exposed by the RuneLite client. No data is stored, cached, uploaded, or sent to custom services.
+
+## Manual RuneLite testing checklist
+
+1. Start the plugin with `./gradlew run --no-daemon --args='--developer-mode --debug'`.
+2. Confirm the external plugin appears as `Smart Hiscore Lookup` in the RuneLite plugin panel.
+3. Log in to a test account and verify the optional chat reminder appears once the client reaches `LOGGED_IN`.
+4. Toggle `Show Login Hint` off and confirm the reminder is suppressed after relogging.
+5. Override `Hiscore Base URL` with a URL that already has a query string and confirm generated links append `&user1=<encoded name>`.
+
+## Plugin Hub prep notes
+
+- Confirm the final GitHub repository URL before plugin-hub submission; `runelite-plugin.properties` currently points at `https://github.com/ItMeansBigMountain/SmartHiscoreLookup`.
+- Capture a screenshot or short GIF from the manual RuneLite test before opening a plugin-hub pull request.
+- If the plugin grows beyond link generation, keep network calls off the game thread and add tests for any parser/cache logic.
